From: atomchild411 <143453386+atomchild411@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WTF: SIMD::findInterleaved's byte halves the right way round
 on big-endian CPUs

DuckDuckGo's results page showed its side menu as raw HTML. The menu is a
template string with a right single quote (U+2019) in it, so it is a
16-bit string, and jQuery turns it into nodes with innerHTML. WebKit's
fast fragment parser scans 16-bit text with SIMD::findInterleaved, which
loads 32 bytes with vld2q_u8 and passes val[0] as the characters' low
bytes and val[1] as their high bytes. vld2q_u8 splits bytes in memory
order, so on a big-endian CPU (IRIX on MIPS) val[0] holds the high
bytes: no '<', '&', '\r' or NUL was ever found in text of 16 characters
or more, and the whole fragment became one text node. Shorter text takes
the scalar loop and was right, which is why most pages were fine.

The load now swaps the two halves back on big-endian CPUs. Both users
(scanText and attribute values in HTMLDocumentParserFastPath) get the
low bytes in val[0] again. Checked with the scan built for IRIX against
WebKit's SIMDe: the original load finds no '<' in a 16-bit
"<div ...>" string, the swapped one finds it at 0.

Fixes https://github.com/atomchild411/heliotrope/issues/1

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/SIMDHelpers.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/SIMDHelpers.h
@@ -621,15 +621,26 @@
 {
     constexpr size_t stride = SIMD::stride<CharacterType> * 2;
     static_assert(threshold >= stride);
+    // Each character's bytes, split into two vectors: val[0] the low bytes
+    // and val[1] the high bytes, which is what the vectorMatch functions take.
+    // vld2q_u8 deinterleaves in memory order, so on a big-endian CPU the high
+    // byte comes first and the two halves are swapped back.
+    auto load = [](const CharacterType* pointer) ALWAYS_INLINE_LAMBDA {
+        auto bytes = simde_vld2q_u8(std::bit_cast<const uint8_t*>(pointer));
+#if CPU(BIG_ENDIAN)
+        std::swap(bytes.val[0], bytes.val[1]);
+#endif
+        return bytes;
+    };
     const auto* cursor = span.data();
     const auto* end = span.data() + span.size();
     if (span.size() >= threshold) {
         for (; cursor + stride <= end; cursor += stride) {
-            if (auto index = vectorMatch(simde_vld2q_u8(std::bit_cast<const uint8_t*>(cursor))))
+            if (auto index = vectorMatch(load(cursor)))
                 return cursor + index.value();
         }
         if (cursor < end) {
-            if (auto index = vectorMatch(simde_vld2q_u8(std::bit_cast<const uint8_t*>(end - stride))))
+            if (auto index = vectorMatch(load(end - stride)))
                 return end - stride + index.value();
         }
         return end;
